WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.600
Head over to Theme Studio.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:07.400
From there, click on AI Asset Creator.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:13.200
Here, you'll be greeted with three different asset categories: Background, outfit, and pose.

4
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.500
We're using Gemini today, but any generative AI model will work.

5
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.600
To keep things simple, I'll follow the exact example prompt from the guide.

6
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:40.750
Next, copy the outfit description generated by your AI, and paste it directly into the variable description box.

7
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.200
Click on the "Generate with ComfyUI" button, and wait.

8
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:05.550
Don't forget to copy over the background title and short description, then paste them into their respective fields.

9
00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:26.400
Finally, click on "Accept and Save to Asset Library" to complete your new background.

10
00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.000
Now let's move on to creating our outfits.

11
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.500
Once again, we'll be using the example prompt from the guide.

12
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:40.500
While it's not shown here, you can use the drop-down menu to toggle between male and female outfits.

13
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.800
But we'll stick with female for now.

14
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.400
The workflow is very similar to setting up the background,

15
00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.100
just with a couple of extra steps.

16
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.500
Finally, let's set up the poses.

17
00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:22.200
Once again, we'll grab the example prompt from the guide, but feel free to get creative with your own.

18
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.500
Just be sure to double check that your prompt starts with "facing the camera with",

19
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:30.100
and that none of the poses cover or block the face.

20
00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:15.300
You can review everything you've made by going to the Asset Gallery, where your assets are split into three distinct categories.

21
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.500
Now let's add our newly created assets to a theme.

22
00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.100
For this example, we'll be using the Deepavali theme.

23
00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:05.100
And there you have it! You're now ready to create your own backgrounds, outfits, and poses.